<rml>
<head>
	<!-- Loading screen: replaces the legacy loading window (uiscript
	     loadingwindow.py) while the loading flag is on (controller:
	     assets/root/nui_loading.py, LoadingWindow subclasses
	     introLoading.LoadingWindow, which keeps the load steps). Full screen
	     and opaque; it never takes the mouse. The background is one of the
	     legacy loading images, stretched as legacy stretches it; the emblem
	     is the legacy ani_image sequence (24 frames, one per 60 Hz frame) as
	     a nui-frames element; the gauge shows the load progress at once.
	     The error line shows when a load step failed. No data events.
	     Modern frames the emblem and the gauge as a board (the gauge panel
	     of the reviewed design) and adds the gauge's quarter marks and the
	     progress in percent; classic hides them and shows the legacy art
	     alone. -->
	<title>loading</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="loading.rcss"/>
</head>
<body template="nui" class="nui-overlay loading" data-model="loading">
	<img class="loading-background" data-attr-src="background" data-if="background != ''"/>
	<div id="loading-board" class="nui-board nui-fx loading-board">
		<nui-frames id="loading-frames" class="loading-frames" count="24" delay="0.0167"/>
		<span class="loading__track"></span><span class="loading__hole"></span>
		<span id="loading-ring" class="loading__ring nui-anim"><span class="loading__dot"></span></span>
		<progress id="loading-gauge" class="loading-gauge" direction="right" max="100" data-attr-value="progress"/>
		<span class="loading__tick loading__tick--1"></span><span class="loading__tick loading__tick--2"></span><span class="loading__tick loading__tick--3"></span>
		<span class="loading__pct">{{ progress | format(0) }}%</span>
	</div>
	<span id="loading-error" class="loading-error" data-if="error">@ui.LOAD_ERROR</span>
</body>
</rml>
